  "question": {
    "text": "If a wire is stretched to make it $0.1 \\%$ longer, its resistance will :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AVdeP",
      "text": "\nincrease by $0.2 \\%$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "fCOMm",
      "text": "\ndecrease by $0.2 \\%$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CJMcQ",
      "text": "\ndecrease by $0.05 \\%$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t6UbZ",
      "text": "\nincreases by $0.05 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{R} \\propto \\ell^2$ (for a given volume)\n$$\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{R}} \\%=\\frac{2 \\Delta \\ell}{\\ell} \\%\n$$\nThus when wire is stretched by $0.1 \\%$ resistance increases by $0.2 \\%$",
    "image": null
  },
